# Coldwater (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, section 3): the lake's fishers on Glasswater, where the Long River rises. Calm;
# nets, water, weed and catch. Drafts (phase 3), to be written properly with you (phase 7).

grammar coldwater
greet = Still water | Calm water to you
greet.broad = Still water, still water
farewell = Fair winds | Calm water
agree = It'll float | Fair enough
refuse = That won't float
surprise = Well, I'll be netted | Calm, now
annoyed = Weed and tangle | Holed again
very = right
good = fair catch | fair
bad = muddied | rough
worthless = bait | net-weed
luck = a full net
child = minnow
pet!! = little fish | my pearl
rain = lake-rain | wet
tired = waterlogged
nonsense = weed
tag = , eh?
oath! = Deep and dark | Net and line | Glass and gods
home = my own shore
